\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The mesh defect on 6 vertices}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Take the circle mesh of \ref{fdip-00B4} with #{N=3}. The
shape on #{6} vertices is #{1+(\mu)/(72)}, and the shape on
three vertices is #{1+(\mu)/(18)}. That proposition gives
##{T_2\Bigl(1+\frac{\mu}{72}\Bigr)
-\Bigl(1+\frac{\mu}{18}\Bigr)
=\frac{\mu^2}{2592}.}
The difference is positive for every #{\mu>0}.}
